            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-0",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-xl",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "130ch",
            "richtext": "<p>If your skin feels dry, your sinuses are irritated, or static shocks seem unavoidable, indoor humidity may be playing a role. Those looking to improve indoor comfort often turn to humidifiers during colder months, when indoor air naturally dries out.</p><p>In some situations, changes in humidity can take time and may feel more gradual. Indoor humidity is influenced by factors such as climate, outdoor temperatures, airflow, and how a home is built. Understanding these influences can help you optimize how your humidifier is used and experience more<br/>consistent comfort throughout your space.</p><p>Below, Blueair experts explain how humidification works, why results can vary from home to home, and how InvisibleMist™ technology is designed to deliver cleaner, more balanced indoor humidity.</p><h4><strong>What Makes Blueair InvisibleMist™ Unique?</strong></h4><p></p><p>Blueair humidifiers are designed using the same airflow expertise behind our air purifiers, with a focus on clean, balanced, and consistent humidity.</p><p>Unlike mist-based humidifiers, Blueair uses <strong>InvisibleMist™ evaporative technology</strong>, which adds moisture naturally without releasing visible mist into the air. Dry air is quietly drawn into the unit, passed through an anti-microbial wick filter, and released back into the room as clean, invisible humidity.</p><p>Key features include:</p><ul><li><strong>True 360-degree air intake and output</strong>, which helps distribute humidity evenly throughout the room</li><li><strong>Anti-microbial wick filters</strong> designed to help inhibit bacterial growth and reduce odors</li><li><strong>Pump-enabled water delivery</strong>, which separates the water tank from the wick for cleaner operation and reduced mineral buildup</li><li><strong>No visible mist and no white dust</strong>, even when using tap water</li></ul><p></p><p>Together, these features support a more hygienic humidification process and a more comfortable indoor environment.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_QBGK76": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-0",
